<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862).

  ADS 2 does not read RaceProperties or a body type to decide which animals get surgery. It keeps three
  abstract RecipeDefs, ADS_Cat1 (medieval replacements), ADS_Cat2 (+ simple prosthetics) and ADS_Cat3
  (+ bionics), each with a hand-curated <recipeUsers> list, and copies those lists onto the real surgery
  recipes in its own last patch (Patches/z_Category_Patches.xml). An animal absent from all three lists
  offers only amputation and euthanasia, as if the mod were not installed. Neither of ours is listed, so
  without this file ADS 2 is a silent no-op for them.

  Both go into all three categories. The choice follows the animals' vanilla counterparts in ADS 2's own
  list (1.6/Defs/AnimalCategories/Animal_Categories.xml, read 2026-09-28):

    - the meffalo is a muffalo variant, and Muffalo is in Cat1, Cat2 and Cat3;
    - the boomsloth has a megasloth's body (QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail) and a megasloth's size, and
      Megasloth is in Cat1, Cat2 and Cat3. Boomalope is in Cat1 and Cat2 only, but the list follows size
      and strength, not explosiveness: Thrumbo, Elephant and Warg are in all three, Boomalope (body size
      2.0) is not, and the boomsloth is body size 4.0.

  The lists are cumulative, so an animal in Cat3 appears in the other two: the three additions are needed.

  The guard is PatchOperationConditional on ADS_Cat1. Without ADS 2 the xpath selects nothing, no
  <nomatch> is declared, and the operation reports success without logging anything. It is NOT MayRequire:
  MayRequire on an <Operation> is read by nothing (Verse.PatchOperation has no such field), so the
  operation would apply whether ADS 2 is loaded or not. Every branch of the predicate repeats @Name=, since
  [@Name="A" or "B"] is true for every RecipeDef in the document.

  About.xml declares <loadBefore>SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2</loadBefore>: ADS 2 copies the lists
  once, at its own patch, so this patch has to run first or it writes into lists nobody reads any more.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[
				@Name="ADS_Cat3" or
				@Name="ADS_Cat2" or
				@Name="ADS_Cat1"
			]/recipeUsers</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>Meffalo</li>
				<li>Boomsloth</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
